cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ssl-vs-btm-asr"
abstract: >-
  Is it self-supervised pretraining or the Branch-Train-Merge pipeline that
  carries low-resource multilingual ASR? A clean, multi-seed ablation on the
  XEUS encoder across three training conditions, three language scales, and
  four held-out Indic transfer languages.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-04"license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/setsosie/ssl-vs-btm-asr"
keywords:
  - automatic-speech-recognition
  - self-supervised-learning
  - model-merging
  - branch-train-merge
  - multilingual
  - low-resource-languages
authors:
